{
  "$comment": "Round 1 (docs/round-1-contract.md §3, CodeBlock): the BUILT-IN tokenizer every renderer mirrors so a CodeBlock colours the same on every platform (a host may still supply its own tokenizer; its kinds must be the `codeToken` enum). ONE scanner over the source (CRLF → LF), first rule that matches at the position wins: (1) `lineKinds` — at a line start (after spaces/tabs) a listed prefix makes the rest of the line that kind; (2) `lineComment` prefixes → comment to the end of the line; (3) `blockComment` [open, close] pairs → comment through close (or the end); (4) a quote in `strings` → string through the same unescaped quote (`\\` escapes the next char), stopping before a line break unless the quote is in `multiline`; with `keyStrings` a string followed by optional spaces and `:` is a `property`; (5) with `markup`, `<` followed by a letter, `/` or `!` opens a tag: `<`/`</` punctuation, the name `tag`, then whitespace plain, quotes string, `=` operator, names `attribute`, until `>`/`/>` punctuation (text outside tags is plain); (6) numbers (unless `numbers` is false): a digit, or `.` before a digit, then every [0-9A-Za-z_.]; (7) identifiers: [A-Za-z_$] plus `identExtra`, then the same plus digits: `keywords` (lower-cased first when `caseInsensitive`) → keyword; with `keyIdents` followed by spaces and a single `:` → property; followed by spaces and `(` → function; right after a `.` punctuation → property; in `typeNames` or (with `types: capitalized`) starting A–Z → type; else plain; (8) a run of spaces/tabs → plain; (9) a run of `operators` chars → operator; (10) one `punctuation` char → punctuation; (11) anything else, one char → plain. Then tokens split at line breaks into LINES and adjacent tokens of one kind merge; a line's tokens concatenate to exactly its text. src/code.ts is the reference, fixtures/code-tokens.json locks it.",
  "defaults": { "operators": "+-*/%=&|<>!?^~:@#", "punctuation": "()[]{},.;" },
